function makeEntry(row) {
  const e = {};
  e.id = row.id;
  if (row.name) e.name = row.name;        // conditional field -> different shape
  e.score = row.score;
  if (row.flagged) e.flag = true;          // late conditional field
  if (row.country === 'DE') e.region = 'eu';
  return e;
}

model.en:
Initialize EVERY property unconditionally, in a fixed order, in one constructor — use defaults (<code>null</code>/<code>0</code>/<code>false</code>) instead of conditionally omitting fields, so all objects walk the same transition path and land on one hidden class:<br><code>function makeEntry(row) {
  return {
    id: row.id,
    name: row.name ?? null,
    score: row.score,
    flag: row.flagged === true,
    region: row.country === 'DE' ? 'eu' : null,
  };
}</code><br>Key moves: no conditional property addition, no late additions after creation, consistent key order, and assign <code>null</code> rather than <code>delete</code> for absent fields. An object literal with all keys present is itself the stable shape — V8 caches the leaf hidden class once and every entry reuses it, keeping the access site monomorphic.

